# Fixed defect 129, 2026-09-28, class (B). Symptom: a join wrote `-` against a
# string, `x = a` over `- "s"` joined to `x = a - "s"` and `x = a -` over `"s"`
# to the same, each `certain`, and `check --apply` wrote a `bad_operand`
# program; the coordinator's witness, `0 => 5` over `-` over `"=>"`, is in the
# unit tests. Cause: a join wrote an operator against a literal it takes under
# no type. A join is `certain` now only where its operator takes the literal
# it is written against (`selfhost/operand_families.hero`, the checker's own
# answers), so these are a `guess`.
#
# A golden cannot hold a `guess`: this `.expected` is `--brief`, which prints
# no certainty, and a `.fixed` must check clean. So what this file pins is one
# diagnostic per break; the certainties are held by `selfhost/lexer.hero`'s
# defect 129 tests, which lex the same shapes.

function at_the_head(a: i64) -> i64
    x = a
    - "s"  #~ continuation_outside_brackets
    return x

function at_the_end(a: i64) -> i64
    #~v continuation_outside_brackets
    x = a -
    "s"
    return x

function in_an_arm(n: i64) -> i64
    return match n
        0 => 5
        - "=>"  #~ continuation_outside_brackets
        _ => 20

function main()
    print(at_the_head(a: 1) + at_the_end(a: 1) + in_an_arm(n: 0))
